 "issue": 1960,
 "issue_title": "Bug: preserve empty pandas int64 dtype in from_pandas",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`from_pandas()` loses regular pandas integer dtype information for zero-row DataFrames. An empty `int64` column is converted to an Arnio `string` column, and `to_pandas()` then returns it as `string` instead of preserving numeric intent.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEmpty DataFrames are common in filtered pipelines, smoke tests, and schema-first workflows. If Arnio changes an empty integer column into a string column, downstream schema validation, dtype-based selection, and pandas interoperability can behave differently depending only on whether the current batch has rows.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `from_pandas()` passes `dtype_hints` to `_Frame.from_dict(..., len(df))`.\n- `arnio/convert.py`: `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` maps nullable `pd.Int64Dtype()` but does not map regular NumPy/pandas `int64` for empty columns.\n- With no values present, the native frame cannot infer `int64` from data, so the column falls back to `string`.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nsource = pd.DataFrame({\"id\": pd.Series([], dtype=\"int64\")})\nframe = ar.from_pandas(source)\n\nprint(frame.shape)\n# (0, 1)\n\nprint(frame.dtypes)\n# Actual: {'id': 'string'}\n\nprint(ar.to_pandas(frame).dtypes.astype(str).to_dict())\n# Actual: {'id': 'string'}\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`from_pandas()` should preserve supported empty-column dtype hints consistently. For a zero-row `int64` pandas column, Arnio should create an `int64` column and round-trip it back as an integer dtype where supported.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe empty `int64` column becomes an Arnio `string` column.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nExtend `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` to recognize regular pandas/NumPy integer dtypes such as `int64` when they are supported by Arnio, and add regression tests for zero-row `int64`, nullable `Int64`, `float64`, `bool`, and `string` columns.\n\n## References\n\n- Relevant file: `arnio/convert.py`\n- Related broad area: pandas interoperability and zero-row frame correctness\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1960",
 "pr": 2492,
 "pr_title": "fix: preserve empty pandas int64 dtype in from_pandas",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes the bug where `from_pandas()` loses regular numpy `int64` dtype information for zero-row DataFrames. An empty `int64` column was being converted to an Arnio `string` column, causing `to_pandas()` to return it as `string` instead of `Int64`.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\n`_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` in `arnio/convert.py` handled nullable `pd.Int64Dtype()` but did not handle regular numpy `int64`. With no values present, the native frame could not infer the dtype from data, so the column fell back to `string`.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nAdded `str(dtype) == \"int64\"` check to `_pandas_dtype_to_arnio()` so the dtype hint is correctly passed to `_Frame.from_dict()` for empty columns.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nAdded `TestEmptyInt64DtypePreservation` in `tests/test_convert.py` covering:\r\n- empty numpy `int64` roundtrip\r\n- empty nullable `Int64` roundtrip\r\n- empty `float64` roundtrip\r\n- empty `bool` roundtrip\r\n- empty `string` roundtrip\r\n- empty mixed schema roundtrip\r\n\r\nCloses #1960",
 "fix_commit": "fce4203904bb1a5e2c32b1cda76a8ee6c8982ad0",
